---
// Cargo Desk: a ten-cycle crude oil trading game, played in the page.
// The markup here matches the game's own index.html, and the browser scripts in
// public/cargo-desk/ are plain browser scripts that find it by id. They run in
// order: rules, historical scenarios, leaderboard, the tape, the tutorial, then the screen code.
// The game is styled entirely with the site's tokens, so it follows the theme.
import '../styles/cargo-desk.css';
---

<section class="cargo-desk" id="cargo-desk" aria-label="Cargo Desk, a crude oil trading game">
  <noscript><p class="cd-noscript">The game runs in your browser and needs JavaScript switched on.</p></noscript>
  <div class="cd-bar">
    <div class="cd-run">
      <span class="label label--ink numeric" id="campaign-progress">Cycle 1 of 10</span>
      <ol class="cd-timeline" id="timeline" aria-label="Campaign progress"></ol>
      <span class="cd-badge" id="run-kind">Ranked run</span>
      <span class="label numeric cd-run__seed" id="seed-value"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="cd-bar__actions">
      <button class="cd-mini cd-weekly-trigger" id="weekly-button" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="weekly-dialog">Weekly challenge</button>
      <button class="cd-mini" id="tutorial-button" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="tutorial-dialog">Tutorial</button>
      <button class="cd-mini" id="help-button" type="button">How to play</button>
      <button class="cd-mini" id="leaderboard-button" type="button">Leaderboard</button>
      <button class="cd-mini cd-mini--solid" id="restart-button" type="button">New run</button>
      <button class="cd-mini" id="weekly-leave" type="button" hidden>Back to campaign</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <aside class="cd-tutorial-prompt" id="tutorial-prompt" aria-labelledby="tutorial-prompt-title" hidden>
    <div>
      <p id="tutorial-prompt-title"><strong>First time at the desk?</strong></p>
      <p>Buy, hedge and deliver oil in three guided steps.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="cd-tutorial-prompt__actions">
      <button class="cd-mini cd-mini--solid" id="tutorial-start" type="button" aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-controls="tutorial-dialog">Start tutorial</button>
      <button class="cd-mini" id="tutorial-dismiss" type="button">Skip for now</button>
    </div>
  </aside>

  <dl class="cells cd-numbers" aria-label="Current book">
    <div class="cell">
      <dt class="label" id="net-label">Marked P&amp;L</dt>
      <dd class="cd-number numeric" id="net-value">$0</dd>
      <dd class="cd-number__note" id="net-detail">Crude + futures + logistics</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <dt class="label">Crude owned</dt>
      <dd class="cd-number numeric" id="crude-value">0</dd>
      <dd class="cd-number__note" id="crude-detail"></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <dt class="label">Net position</dt>
      <dd class="cd-number numeric" id="exposure-value">0</dd>
      <dd class="cd-number__note" id="exposure-detail"></dd>
    </div>
    <div class="cell">
      <dt class="label">Tank A</dt>
      <dd class="cd-number numeric" id="tank-value">0%</dd>
      <dd class="cd-number__note" id="tank-detail"></dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <div class="cd-workspace">
    <section class="cd-terminal" aria-labelledby="terminal-title">
      <div class="cd-card__head">
        <h2 class="label label--marked" id="terminal-title">Terminal</h2>
        <p class="label numeric" id="location-clock"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="cd-flow">
        <div class="cd-node cd-node--in">
          <p class="label">Client inbound</p>
          <p class="cd-node__value numeric" id="inbound-value">None due</p>
          <p class="cd-node__note" id="inbound-note"></p>
        </div>
        <div class="cd-pipe" id="pipe-in" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="cd-tank-wrap">
          <div class="cd-tank" id="tank" role="img" aria-label="Tank A">
            <i class="cd-tank__tick" style="bottom:25%"></i><i class="cd-tank__tick" style="bottom:50%"></i><i class="cd-tank__tick" style="bottom:75%"></i>
            <div class="cd-tank__fill cd-tank__fill--owned" id="tank-owned"></div>
            <div class="cd-tank__fill cd-tank__fill--client" id="tank-client"></div>
            <span class="cd-tank__name label">Tank A</span>
            <span class="cd-tank__pct numeric" id="tank-pct">0%</span>
            <span class="cd-tank__grip" id="tank-grip" aria-hidden="true" hidden></span>
          </div>
          <div class="cd-key-wrap">
          <dl class="cd-key">
            <div><dt><i class="cd-swatch cd-swatch--owned" aria-hidden="true"></i>Your crude</dt><dd class="numeric" id="key-owned">0</dd></div>
            <div><dt><i class="cd-swatch cd-swatch--client" aria-hidden="true"></i>Client crude</dt><dd class="numeric" id="key-client">0</dd></div>
            <div><dt><i class="cd-swatch cd-swatch--free" aria-hidden="true"></i>Free space</dt><dd class="numeric" id="key-free">0</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="cd-key__tag label" id="tank-tag">Now</p>
            <p class="cd-key__hint" id="tank-draft">Drag the tank handle to buy or sell.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cd-pipe" id="pipe-out" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="cd-node cd-node--out">
          <p class="label">Outbound</p>
          <p class="cd-node__value numeric" id="outbound-value"></p>
          <p class="cd-node__note" id="outbound-note"></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cd-overflow">
        <p class="label">Overflow, off-site</p>
        <div class="cd-overflow__bar" aria-hidden="true"><i id="overflow-fill"></i></div>
        <p class="cd-overflow__text" id="overflow-text"></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="cd-card cd-delivery-calendar" aria-labelledby="delivery-title">
      <div class="cd-card__head">
        <h2 class="label label--marked" id="delivery-title">Delivery calendar</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="cd-delivery-position" id="delivery-position">No forward deliveries booked.</p>
      <ol class="cd-delivery-days" id="delivery-days" role="list" aria-label="Delivery cycles" hidden></ol>
      <ul class="cd-delivery-list" id="delivery-list" role="list" aria-label="Booked deliveries" hidden></ul>
      <details class="cd-details" id="delivery-history" hidden>
        <summary id="delivery-history-count">Completed deliveries</summary>
        <ul class="cd-delivery-list" id="delivery-history-list" role="list"></ul>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="cd-card cd-ticket" id="ticket" aria-labelledby="decision-title">
      <div class="cd-card__head">
        <h2 class="label label--marked" id="decision-label">Order ticket</h2>
        <p class="label numeric" id="phase">Cycle 1</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-last" id="cycle-note" aria-live="polite" hidden>
        <p class="label" id="cycle-headline"></p>
        <p class="cd-last__news" id="cycle-news" hidden></p>
        <p class="cd-last__line"><span id="cycle-outcome"></span><strong class="numeric" id="cycle-delta"></strong></p>
        <p class="cd-last__why numeric" id="cycle-why"></p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-brief">
        <p class="label label--accent" id="decision-desk"></p>
        <h3 id="decision-title" tabindex="-1"></h3>
        <p id="decision-brief"></p>
        <p class="cd-brief__market" id="market-note" hidden></p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-watch" id="briefing" hidden>
        <p class="cd-watch__head"><span class="label label--accent" id="briefing-when"></span><span class="label label--ink">Real prices</span></p>
        <p class="cd-watch__detail" id="briefing-intro" hidden></p>
        <p class="cd-watch__title" id="briefing-text"></p>
      </div>

      <div class="cd-watch" id="watch" hidden>
        <p class="cd-watch__head"><span class="label label--accent" id="watch-when">On watch tonight</span><span class="label label--ink numeric" id="watch-odds"></span></p>
        <div class="cd-watch__meter" aria-hidden="true"><i id="watch-meter"></i></div>
        <p class="cd-watch__title" id="watch-title"></p>
        <p class="cd-watch__detail" id="watch-detail"></p>
        <p class="cd-watch__revised numeric" id="watch-revised" hidden></p>
        <dl class="cd-watch__cases">
          <div><dt class="label">If it happens</dt><dd class="numeric" id="watch-hit"></dd></div>
          <div><dt class="label">If it does not</dt><dd class="numeric" id="watch-miss"></dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <form id="decision-form" novalidate>
        <dl class="cells cd-quotes" aria-label="Quotes in dollars per barrel">
          <div class="cell"><dt class="label">Local bid</dt><dd class="numeric" id="ticket-bid">–</dd></div>
          <div class="cell"><dt class="label">Local ask</dt><dd class="numeric" id="ticket-ask">–</dd></div>
          <div class="cell"><dt class="label">Spot</dt><dd class="numeric" id="ticket-spot">–</dd></div>
          <div class="cell"><dt class="label" id="ticket-front-label">Dec futures</dt><dd class="numeric" id="ticket-front">–</dd></div>
        </dl>

        <fieldset id="order-ticket" class="cd-fields">
          <legend class="visually-hidden">Orders for this cycle</legend>

          <fieldset class="cd-step" id="client-step" hidden>
            <legend><span class="cd-step__n numeric" aria-hidden="true">01</span>Client delivery <span class="cd-step__aside numeric" id="client-volume"></span></legend>
            <div class="cd-choices cd-choices--stack" id="client-choices">
              <label class="cd-choice"><input type="radio" name="client" value="accept"><span><b>Accept</b><small id="client-accept-detail"></small></span></label>
              <label class="cd-choice"><input type="radio" name="client" value="defer"><span><b>Reschedule</b><small id="client-defer-detail"></small></span></label>
              <label class="cd-choice"><input type="radio" name="client" value="redirect"><span><b>Turn away</b><small id="client-redirect-detail"></small></span></label>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset class="cd-step">
            <legend><span class="cd-step__n numeric" aria-hidden="true" data-step-number>02</span>Physical crude</legend>
            <div class="cd-choices" id="side-choices">
              <label class="cd-choice"><input type="radio" name="side" value="hold" checked><span><b>Hold</b></span></label>
              <label class="cd-choice"><input type="radio" name="side" value="buy"><span><b>Buy</b></span></label>
              <label class="cd-choice"><input type="radio" name="side" value="sell"><span><b>Sell locally</b></span></label>
              <label class="cd-choice"><input type="radio" name="side" value="ship"><span><b>Ship to Gulf</b></span></label>
              <label class="cd-choice cd-choice--emergency" id="emergency-choice" hidden><input type="radio" name="side" value="emergency" disabled><span><b>Emergency sale</b></span></label>
            </div>
            <div class="cd-row">
              <label class="cd-input" for="order-barrels">
                <span class="label">Volume</span>
                <span class="cd-input__box"><input id="order-barrels" name="barrels" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1" value="0" aria-describedby="order-quote"><span aria-hidden="true">bbl</span></span>
              </label>
              <button class="cd-mini" id="barrels-max" type="button">Max</button>
            </div>
            <input class="cd-range" id="order-barrels-range" type="range" min="0" max="0" step="100" value="0" aria-label="Crude volume, by slider">
            <p class="cd-hint" id="order-quote"></p>
            <div class="cd-haggle" id="haggle" hidden>
              <p class="cd-haggle__who"><b id="haggle-name"></b> <span id="haggle-line"></span></p>
              <ol class="cd-haggle__log" id="haggle-log" aria-live="polite"></ol>
              <div class="cd-haggle__ask" id="haggle-ask">
                <label class="label" for="haggle-range" id="haggle-label">Ask for more</label>
                <input class="cd-range" id="haggle-range" type="range" min="5" max="80" step="5" value="20">
                <p class="cd-haggle__price numeric" id="haggle-price"></p>
                <div class="cd-haggle__buttons">
                  <button class="cd-mini cd-mini--solid" id="haggle-send" type="button">Make the offer</button>
                  <button class="cd-mini" id="haggle-take" type="button" hidden></button>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset class="cd-step" id="delivery-step" hidden>
            <legend><span class="cd-step__n numeric" aria-hidden="true" data-step-number></span>Forward delivery</legend>
            <label class="cd-delivery-toggle"><input type="checkbox" id="delivery-enabled" aria-controls="delivery-options"> <span>Book a delivery for a later cycle</span></label>
            <fieldset class="cd-delivery-fields" id="delivery-options" disabled hidden>
              <legend class="visually-hidden">Forward delivery details</legend>
              <div class="cd-delivery-grid">
                <label class="cd-input" for="delivery-cycle"><span class="label">Deliver on</span><select id="delivery-cycle"></select></label>
                <label class="cd-input" for="delivery-barrels">
                  <span class="label">Volume</span>
                  <span class="cd-input__box"><input id="delivery-barrels" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="1" step="1" aria-describedby="delivery-available delivery-error"><span aria-hidden="true">bbl</span></span>
                </label>
                <label class="cd-input" for="delivery-route"><span class="label">Route</span><select id="delivery-route"><option value="local">Sell locally</option><option value="gulf">Ship to Gulf</option></select></label>
                <label class="cd-input" for="delivery-month"><span class="label">WTI price reference</span><select id="delivery-month"></select></label>
              </div>
              <p class="cd-hint" id="delivery-available"></p>
              <dl class="cd-delivery-quote">
                <div><dt class="label">Fixed price</dt><dd><span id="delivery-price">–</span><small id="delivery-basis"></small></dd></div>
                <div><dt class="label">Delivery tariff</dt><dd id="delivery-tariff">–</dd></div>
                <div><dt class="label">Margin vs. spot after costs</dt><dd id="delivery-margin">–</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <p class="cd-hint" id="delivery-after" hidden></p>
              <p class="cd-hint" id="delivery-storage"></p>
              <p class="cd-hint">Booked barrels stay in storage until delivery. Hedge the remaining uncommitted crude.</p>
              <p class="cd-notice" id="delivery-error" hidden></p>
            </fieldset>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset class="cd-step" id="storage-step">
            <legend><span class="cd-step__n numeric" aria-hidden="true" data-step-number>03</span>Overflow storage <button class="cd-mini cd-step__action" id="storage-open" type="button" hidden>Book space</button></legend>
            <div class="cd-row cd-row--two">
              <label class="cd-input" for="order-storage">
                <span class="label">Book</span>
                <span class="cd-input__box"><input id="order-storage" name="storage" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="0" step="1" value="0" aria-describedby="storage-quote"><span aria-hidden="true">bbl</span></span>
              </label>
              <label class="cd-input" for="order-storage-cycles">
                <span class="label">For</span>
                <span class="cd-input__box"><input id="order-storage-cycles" name="storageCycles" type="number" inputmode="numeric" min="1" step="1" value="1" aria-describedby="storage-quote"><span aria-hidden="true">cycles</span></span>
              </label>
            </div>
            <p class="cd-hint" id="storage-quote"></p>
          </fieldset>

          <fieldset class="cd-step">
            <legend><span class="cd-step__n numeric" aria-hidden="true" data-step-number>04</span>WTI futures <button class="cd-mini cd-step__action" id="hedge-flat" type="button">Hedge to flat</button></legend>
            <table class="cd-futures">
              <caption class="visually-hidden">Futures orders by delivery month. A negative number sells.</caption>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Open</th><th scope="col">Order, lots</th><th scope="col">After</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody id="futures-rows"></tbody>
            </table>
            <button class="cd-mini cd-months" id="months-open" type="button" aria-controls="futures-rows" hidden>All months</button>
                  <p class="cd-hint" id="hedge-hint"></p>
            <p class="cd-notice" id="hedge-status" role="status" hidden></p>
            <p class="cd-notice" id="quote-status" hidden></p>
            <p class="cd-notice" id="expiry-note" hidden></p>
            <p class="cd-hint cd-hedge-status" id="hedge-shortcut-status" role="status" hidden></p>
          </fieldset>
        </fieldset>

        <div class="cd-review" id="order-review">
          <dl aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
            <div><dt class="label">Crude after</dt><dd id="order-position">–</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="label">Net position</dt><dd><span id="order-exposure">–</span><span class="cd-gauge" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><b id="gauge-marker"></b></span></dd></div>
            <div><dt class="label" id="scenario-label">If prices move</dt><dd id="order-scenario">–</dd></div>
            <div><dt class="label">Logistics</dt><dd id="order-fees">–</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <div class="cd-commitbar">
            <p class="cd-message" id="order-error" role="status" hidden></p>
            <button class="btn cd-commit" id="confirm-button" type="submit" disabled>Commit orders</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </form>

      <div class="cd-debrief" id="debrief" hidden></div>
    </section>

    <section class="cd-card cd-curve" aria-labelledby="curve-title">
      <div class="cd-card__head">
        <h2 class="label label--marked" id="curve-title">WTI forward curve</h2>
        <p class="label" id="curve-shape"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="cd-chart" id="chart-wrap">
        <canvas id="price-chart" role="img" aria-label="WTI forward curve"></canvas>
      </div>
      <div class="cells cd-quotes cd-quotes--curve" role="group" aria-label="Forward prices" id="quotes"></div>
      <p class="cd-hint" id="curve-hint">Solid line: this cycle. Dashed line: the previous cycle. Select a month to enter a futures order.</p>
      <details class="cd-details" id="wire" hidden>
        <summary>Market wire</summary>
        <ol class="cd-list" id="wire-list"></ol>
      </details>
    </section>

    <section class="cd-card cd-ledger" aria-labelledby="ledger-title">
      <div class="cd-card__head">
        <h2 class="label label--marked" id="ledger-title">Trade ledger</h2>
        <p class="label" id="ledger-status">Open book</p>
      </div>
      <table class="cd-table">
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Profit and loss by component</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Component</th><th scope="col">Position</th><th scope="col" class="num">P&amp;L</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="ledger-rows"></tbody>
      </table>
      <details class="cd-details" id="futures-ledger">
        <summary>Futures by month</summary>
        <table class="cd-table">
          <caption class="visually-hidden">Position and profit and loss by delivery month</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Month</th><th scope="col">Position</th><th scope="col" class="num">P&amp;L</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="futures-ledger-rows"></tbody>
        </table>
      </details>
      <details class="cd-details" id="storage-ledger">
        <summary>Storage and clients</summary>
        <ul class="cd-list" id="storage-list"></ul>
      </details>
      <details class="cd-details" id="activity" hidden>
        <summary>Every entry</summary>
        <ol class="cd-list cd-list--entries" id="activity-list"></ol>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="cd-foot label" id="foot-note">Simulated terminal and prices · All times Central · 1 lot = 1,000 bbl</p>
</section>

<dialog class="cd-dialog cd-weekly" id="weekly-dialog" aria-labelledby="weekly-title" aria-describedby="weekly-intro" data-weekly-origin="https://cargo-desk-weekly-scores.satohj412.chatgpt.site">
  <form method="dialog"><button class="cd-dialog__close" type="submit" aria-label="Close weekly challenge">×</button></form>
  <h2 id="weekly-title" tabindex="-1">Weekly challenge</h2>
  <p id="weekly-intro">Trade the same ten-cycle market as everyone else. Share your score to see where you rank.</p>
  <div class="cd-weekly__period" id="weekly-period" hidden>
    <p class="cd-weekly__dates" id="weekly-dates"></p>
    <p id="weekly-reset"></p>
  </div>
  <p class="cd-weekly__status" id="weekly-status" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
  <div class="cd-weekly__actions">
    <button class="btn" id="weekly-start" type="button" hidden>Start weekly challenge</button>
    <button class="cd-mini" id="weekly-retry" type="button" hidden>Try again</button>
  </div>
  <form class="cd-weekly__share" id="weekly-share" aria-labelledby="weekly-share-title" hidden>
    <h3 class="label label--marked" id="weekly-share-title">Share your weekly score</h3>
    <p>Your username, P&amp;L and drawdown will be public. The game sends your order history to verify the result.</p>
    <label for="weekly-name" class="cd-weekly__name"><span class="label">Username</span><input id="weekly-name" name="username" maxlength="48" autocomplete="username" required></label>
    <label class="cd-weekly__consent"><input id="weekly-consent" type="checkbox" required> <span>Show my score on the public leaderboard</span></label>
    <button class="btn" id="weekly-publish" type="submit">Publish score</button>
  </form>
  <p class="cd-weekly__published" id="weekly-published" hidden></p>
  <div class="cd-weekly__standings" id="weekly-standings" hidden>
    <h3 class="label label--marked">This week’s standings</h3>
    <p id="weekly-empty" hidden>No scores have been shared yet.</p>
    <div class="cd-weekly__table-wrap" id="weekly-table-wrap" hidden>
      <table class="cd-table cd-weekly__table">
        <caption class="visually-hidden">Shared weekly challenge scores</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Rank</th><th scope="col">Username</th><th scope="col" class="num">P&amp;L</th><th scope="col" class="num">Drawdown</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody id="weekly-scores"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog id="tutorial-dialog" class="cd-dialog cd-dialog--narrow cd-tutorial" aria-labelledby="tutorial-title" aria-describedby="tutorial-instruction">
  <form method="dialog"><button class="cd-dialog__close" id="tutorial-close" type="submit" aria-label="Close tutorial">×</button></form>
  <header class="cd-tutorial__header">
    <div>
      <p class="label label--marked">Practice tutorial</p>
      <p class="cd-badge" id="tutorial-step">Step 1 of 3</p>
    </div>
    <progress id="tutorial-progress" aria-label="Tutorial progress" value="1" max="3"></progress>
  </header>
  <h2 id="tutorial-title" tabindex="-1">Buy and hedge crude</h2>
  <p id="tutorial-instruction">Buy crude at the local ask, then sell WTI futures to hedge it. Each futures lot covers 1,000 barrels.</p>
  <div id="tutorial-ticket">
    <fieldset class="cd-tutorial__fields" id="tutorial-trade">
      <legend class="visually-hidden">Crude purchase and futures hedge</legend>
      <p class="cd-tutorial__quote" id="tutorial-trade-quote" hidden></p>
      <div class="cd-tutorial__grid">
        <label for="tutorial-volume"><span class="label">Crude to buy</span><select id="tutorial-volume"></select></label>
        <label for="tutorial-short"><span class="label" id="tutorial-short-label">WTI lots to sell</span><select id="tutorial-short"></select></label>
      </div>
      <details class="cd-tutorial__note">
        <summary>Bid, ask and the hedge</summary>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Bid, ask and spot</dt><dd>The bid is what a local buyer pays you. The ask is what a local seller charges you. Spot is the reference price for crude today.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Short WTI futures</dt><dd>Selling a futures contract opens a short position in that month. One lot covers 1,000 barrels. If futures fall before you buy it back, the hedge gains and can offset a drop in the value of your crude.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Net exposure</dt><dd>Add the uncommitted barrels in lots to your signed futures positions. The starting 6,000 barrels and six short lots net to zero. A flat book can still gain or lose when spot and futures move by different amounts.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </details>
    </fieldset>
    <fieldset class="cd-tutorial__fields" id="tutorial-booking" hidden>
      <legend class="visually-hidden">Forward sale and futures close</legend>
      <div class="cd-tutorial__grid">
        <label for="tutorial-delivery-volume"><span class="label">Crude to book</span><select id="tutorial-delivery-volume"></select></label>
        <label for="tutorial-route"><span class="label">Delivery route</span><select id="tutorial-route"><option value="local">Sell locally</option><option value="gulf">Ship to Gulf</option></select></label>
        <label for="tutorial-month"><span class="label">WTI reference</span><select id="tutorial-month"></select></label>
        <label for="tutorial-buyback"><span class="label" id="tutorial-buyback-label">WTI futures order</span><select id="tutorial-buyback"></select></label>
      </div>
      <p class="cd-tutorial__quote" id="tutorial-quote"></p>
      <details class="cd-tutorial__note">
        <summary>How the delivery price is set</summary>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>Fixed sale and WTI reference</dt><dd>The delivery takes place in cycle 3. The WTI reference sets the sale price today. The futures order adjusts the month you traded in step 1. Buying adds long exposure. Selling adds short exposure.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Route, basis and tariff</dt><dd>Local delivery sells at Cushing. Gulf delivery uses a pipeline. The route’s basis adds to or subtracts from the WTI reference. A pipeline tariff reduces what you receive per barrel.</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </details>
    </fieldset>
    <p class="cd-tutorial__quote" id="tutorial-settlement" hidden></p>
    <details class="cd-tutorial__note" id="tutorial-settle-note" hidden>
      <summary>Storage and client cargo</summary>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Reserved barrels</dt><dd>Booked barrels stay in storage until delivery, count towards tank capacity and are reserved for that buyer. Settling the sale frees that space.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Rent, clients and overflow</dt><dd>Tank A holds 10,000 barrels and the desk pays its lease each cycle. Clients pay to store their own crude, which uses the same space. In the full game, you can book overflow for several cycles or pay to reschedule or turn away a client.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </details>
  </div>
  <section class="cd-tutorial__recap" id="tutorial-recap" aria-label="Profit and loss breakdown" hidden>
    <div class="cd-tutorial__net"><span class="label">P&amp;L this lesson</span><strong class="numeric" id="tutorial-net"></strong></div>
    <dl class="cd-tutorial__rows" id="tutorial-recap-rows"></dl>
    <p class="cd-tutorial__explanation" id="tutorial-explanation"></p>
    <dl class="cd-tutorial__rows cd-tutorial__positions" aria-label="Open positions when the lesson ends">
      <div><dt>Crude still owned</dt><dd id="tutorial-ending-crude"></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Futures still open</dt><dd id="tutorial-ending-futures"></dd></div>
      <div><dt>Net exposure</dt><dd id="tutorial-ending-exposure"></dd></div>
    </dl>
    <details class="cd-tutorial__note">
      <summary>Read P&amp;L and risk</summary>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Marked P&amp;L</dt><dd>The desk values open positions at current prices as well as counting completed trades and fees. The lesson measures the change in that total over three cycles.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Basis P&amp;L</dt><dd>Spot moving differently from futures can move the value of a hedged book. This is separate from the route basis you used to price a delivery.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Drawdown</dt><dd>The largest fall from an earlier P&amp;L peak during a run. A desk can finish profitable after a large drawdown.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </details>
    <details class="cd-tutorial__note">
      <summary>What changes in the full game?</summary>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>New tickets</dt><dd>Review prices, tank space, fees and net exposure before committing each morning. Generated markets can open a shorter afternoon ticket after news. A new run starts a fresh ten-cycle market or opens a historical scenario.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Futures limits and expiry</dt><dd>The desk allows up to two net lots long or short and twenty total open futures lots. A roll closes an expiring contract and opens a later one to keep the hedge. The order ticket flags expiry and offers Roll and hedge.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Calendar spreads</dt><dd>Buy one futures month and sell another to trade the price difference between them. A later price above a nearer price is contango. The reverse is backwardation.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </details>
  </section>
  <div class="cd-tutorial__guide" id="tutorial-guide" hidden>
    <p id="tutorial-suggestion"></p>
    <button class="cd-mini" id="tutorial-flat" type="button">Use flat hedge</button>
  </div>
  <p class="cd-tutorial__feedback" id="tutorial-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
  <div class="cd-tutorial__actions">
    <button class="btn" id="tutorial-next" type="button">Buy and hedge</button>
    <button class="btn" id="tutorial-complete" type="button" hidden>Back to the desk</button>
  </div>
</dialog>

<dialog id="help-dialog" class="cd-dialog" aria-labelledby="help-title">
  <form method="dialog"><button class="cd-dialog__close" aria-label="Close">×</button></form>
  <p class="label label--marked">How to play</p>
  <h2 id="help-title">Run the book for ten cycles</h2>
  <p>Each cycle is one trading day. Fill in the morning ticket and commit, then watch the day trade. In a generated market, midday news can give you a shorter afternoon ticket before the market moves overnight. After cycle ten, the desk closes any open positions and reports the final result.</p>
  <dl class="cd-help">
    <div><dt>What you start with</dt><dd>6,000 barrels of crude in Tank A and six short lots in the front futures month. Generated runs start at $72.20 per barrel with Dec sold at $73.60. Historical runs open at the prior close’s spot and front-month prices. One lot is 1,000 barrels.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>The tank</dt><dd>Tank A holds 10,000 barrels and costs a fixed lease every cycle, full or empty. Clients pay you per barrel to store their crude in it. Anything that does not fit, yours or theirs, needs overflow space booked off-site.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Physical trades</dt><dd>Each ticket can buy crude, sell locally or ship to the Gulf Coast when a pipeline slot is open. If the local buyer walks away and available overflow falls short of existing storage needs, an emergency sale can free the minimum space needed at a worse price.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Forward delivery</dt><dd>On a morning ticket, commit owned crude to a later cycle at a fixed price based on the WTI month you choose and the route's basis. The WTI reference locks the physical sale price today. Reserved barrels count toward storage until delivery, and your futures hedge covers the uncommitted crude. The delivery calendar shows when cargo is due.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Negotiating</dt><dd>A local price is an opening price. You can ask the counterparty for more. If they refuse they come back once with a counter, which you can take, or you can ask one last time. A second refusal and they walk, and that route is closed for the session. How they sound is a guide to how far they will move.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>The afternoon</dt><dd>On days with midday news you get a second, shorter ticket: local trades in half the size at ten cents worse, and futures. Clients and overflow are morning business only.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Contango and backwardation</dt><dd>Contango means futures are above spot. Backwardation means they are below spot. A hedged storage trade can gain as contango narrows. Compare the potential gain with tank rent, overflow costs and your exit bid.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>On watch</dt><dd>Some days an event is on watch for the coming night, with its odds and roughly what it would do to futures and to spot. The odds are honest, but the size of the reaction is not exact, and fresh news at midday can move the odds. The ticket shows what your book would make or lose each way before you commit.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>The stocks report</dt><dd>The weekly stocks report comes out at midday on both Wednesdays. It is close to a coin flip, it moves spot more than futures, and you get the afternoon to react to it.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Expiry and the roll</dt><dd>The ticket flags the expiring front month. Open contracts settle at spot in generated markets and at the recorded final settlement in historical scenarios. Roll and hedge closes the expiring position and adjusts the next listed month within the desk limits.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Shocks</dt><dd>About one day in ten the market is hit by something nobody saw coming, and prices move by several dollars. A shock that moves every price does nothing to a hedged book. One that moves spot hardest hits anyone holding crude, hedged or not.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Historical scenarios</dt><dd>Play seven episodes using daily spot and futures prices from the U.S. Energy Information Administration. Each day trades against the prior close and starts with a briefing on what was known then. The path is fixed, with one ticket per day. Estimated futures prices are display-only. Terminal bids, clients and storage rates are simulated.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Reading the result</dt><dd>After each ticket the desk separates the result into trading, price, basis, calendar spreads, client income and costs. The debrief compares your result with holding the hedged cargo. Generated runs also receive a grade based on the return and drawdown.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>The desk limits</dt><dd>Open crude exposure and futures must stay within two net lots of flat. The futures book can hold twenty gross lots. Hedge to flat adjusts the front-month order as far as those limits allow and leaves the other months alone. To trade a calendar spread, buy one month and sell another.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Ranked and practice runs</dt><dd>The first play of a newly generated market is ranked. Typed seeds, replays and historical scenarios are practice runs. The leaderboard groups earlier scores by the rules they used.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Weekly challenge</dt><dd>Play the same ten-cycle market as everyone else. The week resets Monday at 00:00 UTC. After settlement, choose a username to share your final P&amp;L and drawdown. Higher P&amp;L ranks first, with lower drawdown breaking ties.</dd></div>
  </dl>
  <form method="dialog"><button class="btn">Back to the desk</button></form>
</dialog>

